  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x-1)(x+5)<0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny=(x-1)(x+5)\n$$\n\n \nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/910856b0bf27df0038488fadfdb7dee8a8bd259ffbadf3a1f8c6f44f3a39cb3f.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-5<x<1.$",
